# Form: short handoff

Use to continue one bounded task. Default: the task's authorized temporary area or
tracker, not a permanent report chain. Most handoffs need only the body below; if
explicitly retained as durable knowledge, add the optional passport. Copy only the
selected payload; [metadata](../../references/metadata.md) governs durable records.
Essential: next result, base/dirty/scope, owners/constraints, checks/limits and exact
remainder. Remove irrelevant optional fields; never paste secrets or private logs.

## Optional durable passport

```yaml
---
id: "{{project_id}}-HANDOFF-{{unique_id}}"
title: "{{bounded_task}} — continuation"
kind: handoff
status: draft
created: "{{created_iso_date}}"
updated: "{{updated_iso_date}}"
areas: ["{{affected_area}}"]
summary: "{{next_result_and_current_limit}}"
---
```

## Body payload

```markdown
# Continue {{bounded_task}}

- Result / finish criterion: {{specific_next_outcome_and_stop}}.
- Base / dirty: {{exact_source_and_unrelated_changes_to_preserve}}.
- Allowed paths / exclusions: {{finite_write_scope_and_protected_areas}}.
- Sources / owners: {{actual_rule_contract_and_implementation_routes}}.
- Done / evidence: {{actual_result_commands_raw_exits_and_limits}}.
- Required next: {{one_action_or_exact_blocker_owner_and_question}}.
- Review / save authority: {{who_may_accept_write_index_commit_or_publish}}.

This snapshot does not change policy, confer new permissions, or turn a prior PASS
into proof for changed artifacts. Reuse unchanged evidence only after impact analysis.
```

## Optional UI / design payload

Select only the applicable transfer below and place it in the existing task/body.
No new passport, full-product JSON export, or second registry is required.
Use the [UI route](../../skills/pf-ui-design/SKILL.md) and, only for the chosen tool,
the [FigCraft route](../../skills/pf-ui-design/references/figcraft-handoff.md).

```markdown
## UI transfer: {{researcher_to_designer_or_designer_to_developer}}

- Work / result / direction: {{work_mode_result_depth_and_direction_independently}}.
- Finite scope / stop: {{surfaces_meaningful_states_selected_transitions_and_finish}}.
- Source / design revision: {{actual_edition_surface_and_real_node_ids_or_unambiguous_links}}.
- Research → design, if applicable: {{observed_state_labels_control_types_order_visibility_data_units_assets_constraints_and_unknowns}}.
- Design → development, if applicable: {{accepted_layout_states_components_instances_tokens_assets_and_allowed_native_differences}}.
- Resources / rights: {{fonts_icons_text_catalogs_provenance_licenses_and_real_paths}}.
- Shown / executed: {{prepared_states_rules_selected_prototype_actions_and_real_operations_separately}}.
- Preserve / behavior: {{action_visible_outcome_values_to_keep_and_size_scroll_rules}}.
- Known implementation link: {{existing_component_data_or_operation_owner_or_explicit_local_gap_without_invented_api}}.
- Evidence / limits: {{structure_render_and_applicable_interactions_or_real_outcomes_with_revision_and_conditions}}.
- Remainder: {{required_not_run_outside_scope_and_branch_not_reached_distinctly_with_prior_failure_preserved}}.
- Next check / owner: {{only_current_scope_required_action_and_authority}}.
```

A visual reference needs inspected editable states and its actual render, not every
Presenter click or a backend run. A selected prototype additionally needs its named
transitions; real-UI claims need the actual application path. Platform notes do not
promote one result to another. Keep raw export, normalized values and maintained code
separate; a later export does not authorize overwriting manual changes.
